.SS "virtual bool Assimp::IOSystem::ComparePaths (const char * one, const char * second) const\fR [virtual]\fP"

.PP
Compares two paths and check whether the point to identical files\&. The dummy implementation of this virtual member performs a case-insensitive comparison of the given strings\&. The default IO system implementation uses OS mechanisms to convert relative into absolute paths, so the result can be trusted\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIone\fP First file 
.br
\fIsecond\fP Second file 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
true if the paths point to the same file\&. The file needn't be existing, however\&. 
.RE
.PP

.PP
Reimplemented in \fBAssimp::DefaultIOSystem\fP, and \fBAssimp::MemoryIOSystem\fP\&.
